BREACHWATCH — What is happening?

Status: 🟠 Confirmed / remediation continuing

Instructure confirmed unauthorized access affecting Canvas and said the attacker exploited an issue involving the platform's Free-for-Teacher environment. The incident affected usernames, email addresses, course names, enrollment information and messages. Instructure said it found no evidence that credentials, course submissions, course content, birth dates, government identification or financial information were compromised.

On May 7, Canvas, Canvas Beta and Canvas Test were temporarily taken offline after users at multiple schools encountered pages modified with messages associated with ShinyHunters. Canvas was restored roughly four hours later.

ShinyHunters claimed data connected to nearly 9,000 schools and approximately 275 million individuals. Those figures remain attacker claims rather than a confirmed InfinityGrid affected-person count.

InfinityGrid is watching for:

confirmed affected-person count
detailed root-cause report
technical explanation of the Free-for-Teacher flaw
exact authorization boundary crossed
whether tenant isolation was bypassed
how support-ticket functionality contributed
whether privileged application access was obtained
final regulatory findings
litigation discovery
independent confirmation that stolen data was actually destroyed
architecture changes replacing Free-for-Teacher
